Spec: Retrail app code

Purpose:
  Feature-first Flutter app: providers are the ViewModel layer, repositories own data sources,
    pure logic lives in the domain layer.

Structure:
  ./main.dart: Process start, database and preferences wiring
  ./app.dart: MaterialApp with theme, localization and router
  ./core: Theme tokens, connectivity and shared widgets
  ./data: Drift database, DAOs and repositories
  ./domain: Pure Dart logic without Flutter
  ./features: One directory per screen area with its providers and widgets
  ./tracking: Ride recording, GPS pipeline, foreground service, Live Activity, countdown cue
  ./map: Live MapLibre map and pre-rendered ride previews
  ./l10n: ARB files and generated localizations

Owns:
  ./main.dart
  ./app.dart
  /test/foundation
  /test/support
  /test/e2e

References:
  /docs/specs/history/01-foundation.md
  /docs/specs/history/08-navigation-shell.md

Must:
  UI is Material 3 (`useMaterial3: true`) and follows Material 3 component conventions.
  Every user-facing string comes from @AppLocalizations with keys in both `app_en.arb` and `app_de.arb`.
  Every colour, shape and text style comes from the theme tokens (@AppColors, @AppShapes, @AppTypography).
  State logic lives in Riverpod providers written by hand; widgets only read state and send intents.
  Each feature has one provider set (`*_providers.dart`) exposing read-only state and intent methods.
  Repositories return Drift streams; providers transform them.
  A class stays at or below 400 lines of code and has one responsibility.
  State classes are immutable with `copyWith`.
  Explicit `abstract interface class` seams exist only where a real alternate or platform implementation exists;
    single-implementation repositories stay concrete; tiny strategy seams such as @NowMs are typedefs.
  Collaborators such as DAOs and clocks are injected through constructors or providers.
  Bottom sheets open through @showAppScrollableSheet or @showAppBottomSheet; confirmations stay dialogs.
  Snack bars are built with @appSnackBar.
  Status-bar icons follow the theme through @ThemeStatusBar; screens with the fixed dark chrome wrap themselves in
    @DarkChromeStatusBar.
  File names are `snake_case.dart`, types `UpperCamelCase`, providers `camelCaseProvider`.

Must not:
  Use code generation for Riverpod providers.
  Reach globally for singletons instead of injecting them.

Forbids:
  Direct Drift or @SharedPreferences access from ./features
  Hex colour literals outside @AppColors
